window.StrictDoc.search.nodesByMid = {"1":{"MID":"39ab7dc1cbf14000b71ed79d6d8fb256","UID":"DBDD001","TITLE":"The replicated clearance log is the operational store and TOML is configuration read at startup","STATEMENT":"The operational store shall be the replicated clearance log, not a separate database. Each committed entry shall hold the command, the resulting decision, and the requirement UID recorded in the audit. The TOML file shall be read at startup and shall not be written by the clearance path. Acceptance is a committed landing whose log entry contains the aircraft and SRS011, and a running node that does not modify the TOML file.\n","RATIONALE":"MIL-STD-498 includes a database description. This CSCI has a log rather than a database management system, and the log schema is that description.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.","_LINK":"DBDD001"},"2":{"MID":"11a8d8b9ab0c43a0b5723d09637a2756","UID":"IDD001","TITLE":"Concrete schemas for IRS001 through IRS004","STATEMENT":"The design shall represent a pilot clearance as a map with aircraft, runway, sequence, kind, wind, and text fields. A neighbor message shall be a tuple of request, accept, reject, or stale with the aircraft identity. The TOML schema shall match IRS003. A log command shall be a tuple of the clearance kind and its arguments. Acceptance is a round trip that encodes one landing clearance and one handoff accept and decodes them to the same fields.\n","RATIONALE":"The interface requirements need one concrete representation so tests can construct messages.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"Erlang maps and tuples are the concrete syntax. They are not a wire standard beyond this CSCI.","_LINK":"IDD001"},"3":{"MID":"03f0e5f09ed94bb6b094e9773dfda464","UID":"IRS001","TITLE":"Pilot clearance content: aircraft identity, runway, sequence, clearance kind, and wind when the clearance needs it","STATEMENT":"The pilot-facing interface shall carry aircraft identity, runway, sequence position when the aircraft is queued, clearance kind, and wind when the airport configuration supplies wind for a takeoff or landing. The readable phrase shall state those same facts in tower wording for runway assignment, sequence, hold short, line up and wait, takeoff, landing, and go-around. Acceptance is a landing clearance whose fields and phrase agree on the aircraft and the runway, and a takeoff clearance that includes the configured wind.\n","RATIONALE":"FAA JO 7110.65 supplies the information content. The interface carries that content without pasting the order.\n","DAL":"B","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Interface","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"Wind is optional in the TOML file. When it is absent, a takeoff phrase omits wind rather than inventing it.","_LINK":"IRS001"},"4":{"MID":"462c0abbf3104fe98ff9783e852af5fe","UID":"IRS002","TITLE":"Neighbor handoff request, accept, reject, and stale marker","STATEMENT":"The inter-airport interface shall carry a handoff request with aircraft identity and runway intent, an accept, a reject, and a stale marker when the link is down. A receiver shall answer accept or reject. A sender shall treat a down link as stale and shall not send a new request on it. Acceptance is a request followed by accept that transfers control, a reject that does not, and a down link that produces a stale marker and no request.\n","RATIONALE":"The neighbor protocol is the only channel whose loss triggers fail-smart behavior.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Interface","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"IRS002"},"5":{"MID":"d61cc9f831b14d8ca9707ff014d2039d","UID":"IRS003","TITLE":"TOML airport and runway schema","STATEMENT":"The configuration interface shall be one TOML document with an airport table containing identity, latitude, longitude, communications distance, computer count, and envelope limits, plus one runway table per runway containing identifier, designation, and independence. A runway may list the identifiers it intersects. Acceptance is the example airport file, which this schema accepts, and the same file with the designation removed, which it rejects.\n","RATIONALE":"One file is the operator interface for retargeting an airport.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Interface","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"Designation is one of arrival, departure, both, or closed.","_LINK":"IRS003"},"6":{"MID":"f2b04e2844e249c0bf49a5917fdf5629","UID":"IRS004","TITLE":"Intra-airport log command for a single clearance decision","STATEMENT":"The intra-airport interface shall submit one clearance decision as one log command containing the aircraft identity, the kind, and the runway when the kind uses a runway. Members shall apply a committed command at the same index to the same previous state. Acceptance is two members that apply one landing command and report the same resulting occupancy.\n","RATIONALE":"The replicated command is the unit of authority inside the airport.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Interface","VERIFICATION":"PropEr","ASSUMPTIONS":"Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.","_LINK":"IRS004"},"7":{"MID":"2aaf15c0561b4f9084d4a2a2c7524dbc","UID":"OCD001","TITLE":"Local tower service replaces the manned tower for one configured airport","STATEMENT":"The AirTrafficControl system shall perform the local tower function for one airport described by that airport configuration. The service shall accept pilot requests for runway assignment, sequence position, landing, takeoff, hold short, line up and wait, and go-around, and it shall answer each request with a clearance or a refusal. Acceptance is a configured airport that issues a runway and a sequence to an aircraft inside its protected volume, and that refuses a request the separation guard rejects.\n","RATIONALE":"A tower replacement is useful only if the same airport can serve ordinary clearances and refuse an unsafe one.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Operational","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"OCD001"},"8":{"MID":"0abcc7d239674d219d9c4eb0e11f9b8b","UID":"OCD002","TITLE":"Neighbor airports coordinate aircraft that cross a shared communications boundary","STATEMENT":"When two airports are inside each other's configured communications distance, they shall exchange the aircraft identity, runway intent, and acceptance state needed to hand an aircraft from one protected volume to the other. A handoff shall complete only after the receiving airport accepts it. Acceptance is a pair of airports inside the configured distance where the sender stops controlling the aircraft only after the receiver has accepted the handoff.\n","RATIONALE":"Coordination is limited to airports that can actually exchange state, which is the boundary between a cluster and a rural field.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Operational","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"OCD002"},"9":{"MID":"6150efb99a7947a98d275268b14957fd","UID":"OCD003","TITLE":"A rural airport keeps working when the outside link is down","STATEMENT":"An airport that loses communication with every neighbor shall keep providing local tower service for aircraft already inside its protected volume, including an airport configured with one computer and no reachable neighbor. It shall not invent a clearance that depends on neighbor state it cannot confirm. Acceptance is a link cut after which a local arrival still receives a runway and a sequence, and a handoff out of the local volume is refused.\n","RATIONALE":"Rural fields must fail smart rather than stop the local tower or pretend the neighbor sky is empty.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Operational","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"OCD003"},"10":{"MID":"d18f82b6e3d24f58844fef1f00f86fc5","UID":"OCD004","TITLE":"Pilots receive FAA tower clearances for runway, sequence, landing, and takeoff","STATEMENT":"Clearances issued to a pilot shall carry the information content required by FAA JO 7110.65 for the tower clearances in this increment: aircraft identity, runway, sequence position when the aircraft is queued, clearance kind, and wind when the clearance kind uses wind. The kinds are runway assignment, sequence, hold short, line up and wait, takeoff, landing, and go-around. Acceptance is a clearance record that contains those fields and a readable phrase that states the same facts without claiming phraseology outside this set.\n","RATIONALE":"The operational authority for wording and runway separation is FAA JO 7110.65, limited to the tower clearances this increment offers.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Operational","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"Phraseology is described by the information it must carry. The order itself is not copied into the requirement.","_LINK":"OCD004"},"11":{"MID":"da4ebdac53e64e26bf152b68ed8f8fb5","UID":"SDD001","TITLE":"OTP supervision tree for one airport group","STATEMENT":"The Tower CSCI shall start under an OTP application and a one-for-one supervisor. The supervisor shall own the configuration loader, the local log, the neighbor monitor, and the clearance service. A child crash shall restart that child without creating a second log. Acceptance is an application start that registers one supervisor, and a killed child that is restarted while the committed log prefix is unchanged.\n","RATIONALE":"Supervision is how a local computer returns a worker without inventing a new authority.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"Erlang process isolation is not claimed as DO-178C robust partitioning.","_LINK":"SDD001"},"12":{"MID":"4d8c7b69a0be42a69d60f6aae40d311e","UID":"SDD002","TITLE":"Clearance state machine and the TLA+ actions that match it","STATEMENT":"The clearance state machine shall use the phases out, queued, hold, occupying, and air. The actions shall be assign, sequence, hold short, line up and wait, takeoff, land, go-around, and handoff, and each action shall match a TLA+ action of the same name in AtcTower. Occupying means the aircraft is inside the protected volume. Acceptance is a review that every Erlang action name appears in the TLA+ spec and that a sampled transition produces the same phase change in both descriptions.\n","RATIONALE":"The design keeps one action vocabulary so the refinement mapping has something to point at.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Refinement","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SDD002"},"13":{"MID":"e18cebab63da4793a37f0676f1980ea6","UID":"SDD003","TITLE":"Refinement mapping from Erlang state to TLA+ state, including open obligations","STATEMENT":"The design shall include a refinement mapping from the Erlang clearance state to the TLA+ variables for phase, runway, sequence, and link status. The mapping shall list the Raft ordered-log assumption and every obligation that TLC and PropEr do not discharge, and those obligations shall remain labeled open. Acceptance is a mapping document linked from this requirement that a reader can use to find each Erlang field in the spec, and that does not describe an open obligation as proved.\n","RATIONALE":"The mapping is derived design evidence. It is not a completed machine-checked refinement proof.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Derived","VERIFICATION":"Refinement","ASSUMPTIONS":"Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved. Open obligations stay open until a later proof discharges them.","_LINK":"SDD003"},"14":{"MID":"aebb96361bec4af7bf5a6e9e739e0255","UID":"SDD004","TITLE":"Consensus assumption: the Raft log is a single ordered history and Raft is not re-proved","STATEMENT":"The local group shall use Ra as the Raft log. The design shall treat a committed Ra index as the single ordered history and shall not include a proof of Raft. Commands shall be submitted only by the current Ra leader. Acceptance is a three-member Ra cluster in one Erlang node that commits one clearance and rejects a command from a follower that is not the leader.\n","RATIONALE":"Re-proving Raft is out of scope. Using a known library keeps the assumption explicit.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.","_LINK":"SDD004"},"15":{"MID":"c6a09e15d72f48569babf6d5054a5171","UID":"SDD005","TITLE":"Fail-smart mode and the stale-neighbor rule","STATEMENT":"Neighbor state shall be a record with a link flag and a stale flag. When the link is down the stale flag shall be set and the handoff action shall be disabled. Local clearance actions shall ignore stale neighbor occupancy when deciding whether a local volume is free. Acceptance is a neighbor record that becomes stale on link loss and a local landing that is still decided only from local occupancy.\n","RATIONALE":"Stale data remains visible for the operator and unusable for reducing separation.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SDD005"},"16":{"MID":"840fb14a676f4bcdad96bec676b994f3","UID":"SDP001","TITLE":"Lifecycle, Wikipedia DID set, tailoring, DAL, Erlang, TLA+, and trace rules","STATEMENT":"The software development plan shall follow DO-178C objectives for the Tower CSCI and shall record lifecycle data with the MIL-STD-498 data item descriptions: Software development plan (SDP), Software installation plan (SIP), Software transition plan (STrP), Operational concept description (OCD), System/subsystem specification (SSS), Software requirements specification (SRS), Interface requirements specification (IRS), System/subsystem design description (SSDD), Software design description (SDD), Database design description (DBDD), Interface design description (IDD), Software test plan (STP), Software test description (STD), Software test report (STR), Software user manual (SUM), Software input/output manual (SIOM), Software center operator manual (SCOM), Computer operation manual (COM), Computer programming manual (CPM), Firmware support manual (FSM), Software product specification (SPS), and Software version description (SVD). SSS is the system specification and SRS is the software specification. Separation, an unsafe clearance, and fail-smart behavior are DAL A. The implementation language is Erlang and the formal model is TLA+. Each requirement fragment names its parents, and each implementing source file names the requirement UID in a comment and in the commit that adds it. This repository records that evidence and does not claim certification authority approval.\n","RATIONALE":"The plan is the contract for which documents exist and how a change points back at a requirement.\n","DAL":"C","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Plan","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"DO-178C supplement DO-333 is the formal-methods guide for the TLA+ evidence. No authority finding is claimed.","_LINK":"SDP001"},"17":{"MID":"827271462c7948c29ec206f9f911c72d","UID":"SDP002","TITLE":"SIOM, SCOM, COM, CPM, and FSM tailored out, with reasons","STATEMENT":"The project shall tailor out the Software input/output manual (SIOM), the Software center operator manual (SCOM), the Computer operation manual (COM), the Computer programming manual (CPM), and the Firmware support manual (FSM). SIOM and SCOM describe a batch or interactive system installed in a computer center, and this tower is not that system. COM and CPM describe operating and programming a general-purpose computer, which is outside the Tower CSCI. FSM describes firmware devices, and this CSCI has no firmware. Acceptance is this requirement stating those five acronyms and the reason each is absent, with the delivered set limited to the remaining descriptions.\n","RATIONALE":"MIL-STD-498 expects the contract to say which descriptions were not ordered. These five do not match the product.\n","DAL":"C","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Plan","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"Tailoring is recorded here so the five acronyms are not forgotten and not replaced by empty manuals.","_LINK":"SDP002"},"18":{"MID":"19b2e3d9e1634014b3caf6198e665838","UID":"SIP001","TITLE":"Install one release on n airport computers and point them at the TOML file","STATEMENT":"Installation shall place the same Tower release on each of the n computers for one airport and shall point every computer at that airport TOML file. The installer shall not start control until the file passes the configuration check. Acceptance is a procedure a support engineer can follow for n equal to 1 and for n equal to 3, with a bad file leaving the computers stopped.\n","RATIONALE":"Installation is per airport and uses the same file the requirements already constrain.\n","DAL":"D","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Plan","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"No separate computer-center install is required.","_LINK":"SIP001"},"19":{"MID":"64cdf11f653b4796a837e75527868896","UID":"SPS001","TITLE":"Delivered tower sources, model, and requirements","STATEMENT":"The product specification shall list the Tower CSCI artifacts delivered in this version: the Erlang modules and tests under apps/atc_tower, the example airport file config/example-airport.toml, the TLA+ specification specs/tla/AtcTower.tla with specs/tla/AtcTower.cfg, the refinement mapping specs/refinement/Mapping.md, and the StrictDoc sources under reqs. The mapping's open obligations remain open. Acceptance is a reader finding each of those paths in the version that this specification describes.\n","RATIONALE":"The product specification is the inventory of what the version contains after the build and the model exist.\n","DAL":"C","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Plan","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"Generated HTML is listed by the version description. Open proof obligations are not closed by this inventory.","_LINK":"SPS001"},"20":{"MID":"80994a0b175e4af0b0ac91c4c22e8d09","UID":"SRS001","TITLE":"Reject invalid TOML and do not control traffic","STATEMENT":"Before the Tower CSCI controls traffic it shall read the airport TOML file and shall refuse to start control when the file is missing, unreadable, or lacks a required airport identity, position, communications distance, computer count, or runway list. A runway entry that lacks an identifier or a designation shall also prevent control. Acceptance is an empty file and a file with a runway and no designation, both of which leave the node with no authority to issue a clearance.\n","RATIONALE":"A bad configuration is not a safe airport, so the node must not become a clearance authority.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The file is TOML. Unknown keys may be ignored. Missing required keys are errors.","_LINK":"SRS001"},"21":{"MID":"93787a92580f4902a3e67482e790b8f1","UID":"SRS002","TITLE":"Use runway designation and independence when assigning a runway","STATEMENT":"The Tower CSCI shall assign a runway only when its designation allows the intended operation: arrival for landing, departure for takeoff, both for either, and closed for neither. A runway marked not independent shall conflict with every other runway that is not independent, and a runway listed as intersecting another shall conflict with that runway. Acceptance is a closed runway that cannot be assigned, a departure-only runway that rejects a landing, and two non-independent runways that cannot be occupied together.\n","RATIONALE":"Designation is the policy in the TOML file. The clearance code must not invent a use the file does not allow.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SRS002"},"22":{"MID":"9193d3974a0340388a4ebdaaa0a50d91","UID":"SRS003","TITLE":"Form the local group of size n, including n equals 1","STATEMENT":"On startup the Tower CSCI shall form a local computer group whose size is the configured n, including a group of one. Each member shall know the group size and its own identity. A node shall not issue clearances until it has joined that group. Acceptance is a one-member group that becomes the authority, and a three-member group that does not issue a clearance from a member that has not joined.\n","RATIONALE":"The group is the unit of local redundancy. One member is the rural case and is still a group.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.","_LINK":"SRS003"},"23":{"MID":"cad077bc0dea459b8729d709a4ea3e97","UID":"SRS004","TITLE":"Replicate clearance state as one ordered log","STATEMENT":"Issued clearances shall be the prefix of one ordered log replicated to the local group. A member shall apply the same command to the same log index as every other member that holds that index. A command that the guard rejects shall not extend the log. Acceptance is two members that, after the same committed prefix, report the same occupancy, and a rejected command that leaves both prefixes unchanged.\n","RATIONALE":"One ordered history is the software view of the single clearance authority.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"PropEr","ASSUMPTIONS":"Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.","_LINK":"SRS004"},"24":{"MID":"357bc4d0e12443e4847921002e2350a0","UID":"SRS005","TITLE":"Select neighbors by communications distance","STATEMENT":"The Tower CSCI shall compute the distance between this airport and each configured candidate and shall mark a candidate as a neighbor only when that distance is less than or equal to the configured communications distance. A candidate with no position shall not become a neighbor. Acceptance is a candidate one unit inside the distance that is selected and a candidate one unit outside that is not.\n","RATIONALE":"Neighbor selection is data, computed from the TOML positions and distance, not a hard-coded airport list in the clearance module.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"Distance is great-circle distance in nautical miles from the configured coordinates.","_LINK":"SRS005"},"25":{"MID":"0b854e427839418d95593167eb7cae90","UID":"SRS006","TITLE":"Complete a handoff only with a reachable neighbor","STATEMENT":"The Tower CSCI shall send a handoff only to a neighbor whose link is up, and it shall remove the aircraft from local control only after that neighbor accepts. A reject or a missing answer shall leave the aircraft under local control. Acceptance is an accepted handoff that drops local control, and a rejected handoff that keeps the aircraft in the local sequence.\n","RATIONALE":"The sender must not drop an aircraft the receiver has not taken.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SRS006"},"26":{"MID":"87b6657a1355400d82cb91c7b7d3d711","UID":"SRS007","TITLE":"On a dead neighbor link, continue local service and refuse dependent clearances","STATEMENT":"When a neighbor link is down, the Tower CSCI shall keep serving aircraft in the local volume and shall refuse a handoff or any clearance whose safety would depend on that neighbor. State last received from that neighbor shall be marked stale and shall not be used to permit a tighter local operation. Acceptance is a down link during which a local landing is still granted when the local guard allows it, a handoff is refused, and stale neighbor occupancy is not treated as empty sky.\n","RATIONALE":"This is the software statement of fail-smart behavior for a partitioned airport.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SRS007"},"27":{"MID":"dd2349f68f6a4a7b998350838d462dbd","UID":"SRS008","TITLE":"Assign a runway only when designation, independence, and occupancy allow it","STATEMENT":"The Tower CSCI shall assign a runway to an aircraft only when the designation allows the requested operation, the runway is not closed, and the assignment does not conflict with an aircraft already occupying that runway or a conflicting runway. The assignment shall record the aircraft, the runway, and the operation. Acceptance is a successful assignment onto an empty both-use runway and a refusal onto that runway while another aircraft occupies a conflicting runway.\n","RATIONALE":"Assignment is the first occupancy decision and it has to obey the same exclusion as a takeoff or landing.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SRS008"},"28":{"MID":"cf66642a2bd34cb5b506ce45967db631","UID":"SRS009","TITLE":"Keep arrival and departure sequence order","STATEMENT":"The Tower CSCI shall keep a sequence per runway and shall grant a landing or takeoff that uses that runway only to the aircraft at the head of the sequence, after any predecessor has left the protected volume. A new sequence request shall append the aircraft. Acceptance is two aircraft sequenced to one runway where the second takeoff or landing is refused until the first is airborne or clear, then granted.\n","RATIONALE":"Queue order is the in-trail rule this increment can check without a wake-turbulence model.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The in-trail gap is the predecessor leaving the protected volume. No time-based wake category is modeled.","_LINK":"SRS009"},"29":{"MID":"c4a1e245775f491786fced4aa1f64053","UID":"SRS010","TITLE":"Issue or refuse takeoff clearance","STATEMENT":"The Tower CSCI shall issue a takeoff clearance only when the aircraft is at the head of a departure-capable runway sequence and the separation guard accepts the transition into the protected volume or through it to airborne. Otherwise it shall refuse. The issued clearance shall name the aircraft, the runway, and the wind from the airport configuration when wind is present. Acceptance is a head aircraft on a departure runway that is cleared, and a second aircraft on that runway that is refused.\n","RATIONALE":"Takeoff is one of the FAA tower clearances and it is also an occupancy transition.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SRS010"},"30":{"MID":"edddeeaf7b504f92be6d109c744ca0f9","UID":"SRS011","TITLE":"Issue or refuse landing clearance","STATEMENT":"The Tower CSCI shall issue a landing clearance only when the aircraft is at the head of an arrival-capable runway sequence and the guard accepts exclusive occupancy of that runway and its conflicts. Otherwise it shall refuse. The issued clearance shall name the aircraft, the runway, and the sequence position. Acceptance is a head arrival cleared to land on an empty arrival runway, and a refusal while that runway is occupied.\n","RATIONALE":"Landing clearance is the arrival half of the same exclusive-volume rule.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SRS011"},"31":{"MID":"e873ae824afe4012b38de56a2a4befb5","UID":"SRS012","TITLE":"Issue hold short, line up and wait, and go-around when needed to keep the runway exclusive","STATEMENT":"The Tower CSCI shall issue hold short when an aircraft may approach a runway but may not enter it, line up and wait when the aircraft may enter and must not roll, and go-around when an aircraft on approach must leave the protected volume without landing. Line up and wait shall be refused when the volume or a conflicting volume is already occupied. Go-around shall remove the aircraft from the protected volume. Acceptance is a held aircraft that is not occupying, a line-up that is refused while the runway is occupied, and a go-around that frees the runway for the next aircraft.\n","RATIONALE":"These three clearances are the control the tower needs to keep the exclusive-volume invariant enforceable.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SRS012"},"32":{"MID":"fcccb8625960487a8fb7f07eb97907e9","UID":"SRS013","TITLE":"Apply the separation guard before any clearance that changes occupancy","STATEMENT":"Before committing a sequence, assignment, hold short, line up and wait, takeoff, landing, or go-around, the Tower CSCI shall evaluate the pure separation transition for that command. Only a transition that returns an accepted next state may be appended to the log. The guard shall be a pure function of the current occupancy, the runway relation, and the link state. Acceptance is a command set on which every accepted command preserves the exclusive-volume invariant and every rejected command leaves the state unchanged.\n","RATIONALE":"The guard is the executable counterpart of the TLA+ next-state relation.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Formal","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment. Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.","_LINK":"SRS013"},"33":{"MID":"b1432f0529424b7b9fd93339dce62325","UID":"SRS014","TITLE":"Refuse operation outside the performance assumptions and the checked envelope","STATEMENT":"The Tower CSCI shall read the configured maximum runways, aircraft, and neighbors and shall refuse to start control when any of those limits exceeds 4 runways, 8 aircraft, or 2 neighbors, or when the loaded picture already exceeds the limit. It shall also refuse a new aircraft that would exceed the aircraft limit. Acceptance is a TOML file with 5 runways that does not start, and an airport at the aircraft limit that refuses one more aircraft.\n","RATIONALE":"The TLC check is finite. The software must not be operated as if the proof were unbounded.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SRS014"},"34":{"MID":"7ae5a87e5a164c3388248d168d6e4be2","UID":"SRS015","TITLE":"Restart a failed local computer without a second clearance authority","STATEMENT":"When a local computer stops and later restarts, it shall rejoin the group by receiving the committed log before it may issue clearances. It shall not issue from a log prefix that the surviving authority has already superseded. Acceptance is a restarted member that matches the survivor occupancy after replay, and that refuses a command while it is still catching up.\n","RATIONALE":"Recovery must not create a second authority with a stale history.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"PropEr","ASSUMPTIONS":"Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.","_LINK":"SRS015"},"35":{"MID":"cb7edee41b7e437f917e906c6f9e5fbf","UID":"SRS016","TITLE":"Record each decision with the requirement UID it carried out","STATEMENT":"The Tower CSCI shall append an audit record for every issued clearance and every refusal. The record shall contain the aircraft identity, the clearance kind, the runway when one was named, the decision, and the requirement UID of the software requirement that authorized that kind of decision. Acceptance is a landing grant whose audit line contains SRS011, and a refusal whose audit line contains the UID of the guard requirement SRS013.\n","RATIONALE":"The audit log is how an operator and a later reader tie a decision back to the requirement.\n","DAL":"C","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"Audit loss is not itself a separation failure. The record is still required for traceability.","_LINK":"SRS016"},"36":{"MID":"81e01b13b75c40458b1e3e70a40dbae5","UID":"SSDD001","TITLE":"Airport, local computers, and neighbor topology, with the two failure domains","STATEMENT":"The system design shall separate two failure domains. Inside an airport, n computers share one ordered log and lose the authority only when they lose a majority. Between airports, a link failure isolates the airports and each continues with local service under the fail-smart rule. A local computer failure shall not be treated as a neighbor-link failure, and a neighbor-link failure shall not by itself remove a local majority. Acceptance is a design trace that names both domains and a test in which a down neighbor leaves the local majority able to clear a local aircraft.\n","RATIONALE":"The two domains fail differently. Mixing them would either stop a healthy local tower or keep using a dead neighbor.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment. Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.","_LINK":"SSDD001"},"37":{"MID":"4027aa72ce3245fe9d3ea734b5f63922","UID":"SSS001","TITLE":"Aircraft shall not occupy the same runway protected volume","STATEMENT":"While an aircraft occupies a runway protected volume, the system shall refuse every other clearance that would place a second aircraft in that volume or in a volume configured as intersecting or dependent. Independent parallel runways are separate volumes. Acceptance is two aircraft and one runway where the second line-up, landing, or takeoff is refused until the first aircraft is airborne or clear, and the same refusal across a configured conflict pair.\n","RATIONALE":"Loss of runway separation is the catastrophic condition this increment exists to prevent.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Formal","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SSS001"},"38":{"MID":"ec77731e92aa4020a6279abe94bfa9e5","UID":"SSS002","TITLE":"Each airport shall run on n ATC computers for integer n greater than 0","STATEMENT":"Each airport shall be configured with an integer computer count n greater than 0 and shall start a local clearance group of that size. A configuration of one computer is a valid rural airport and shall still apply the separation guard. Acceptance is a startup with n equal to 1 that serves local traffic, and a startup that rejects n less than 1.\n","RATIONALE":"Redundancy is configured per airport. One computer must remain a legal and safe configuration.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SSS002"},"39":{"MID":"3817c809da61470ea16629d73648fac2","UID":"SSS003","TITLE":"Airports inside communications distance shall exchange the state a handoff requires","STATEMENT":"An airport shall treat another airport as a neighbor only when the distance between their configured positions is within the configured communications distance, and it shall exchange handoff requests with such a neighbor. Airports farther apart shall not be offered a handoff. Acceptance is three airports where only the pair inside the distance can complete a handoff.\n","RATIONALE":"Communications distance is the policy that decides who is in the cluster.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment. Positions are the configured latitude and longitude.","_LINK":"SSS003"},"40":{"MID":"23afbfff279c491aa68df1aa7cdc4061","UID":"SSS004","TITLE":"Loss of the outside link shall fail smart and preserve local separation","STATEMENT":"When an airport can no longer exchange traffic state with a neighbor inside the configured communications distance, the local computers shall keep runway assignment, sequencing, landing, and takeoff service for aircraft already inside that airport's protected volume. The airport shall not issue a handoff or any other clearance that depends on neighbor state it cannot confirm. Last-known neighbor data shall stay marked stale and shall not reduce local separation. Coordinated handoffs shall resume only after the neighbor link is revalidated. This shall hold for a rural airport with one computer and no reachable neighbor.\n","RATIONALE":"Fail smart means the local tower continues and unconfirmed neighbor state cannot make a local clearance look safer.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SSS004"},"41":{"MID":"d52e8f979cc2457fa49f26110754794a","UID":"SSS005","TITLE":"The tower shall give runway assignment, sequence, landing, takeoff, hold short, line up and wait, and go-around","STATEMENT":"The tower shall offer runway assignment, sequence position, hold short, line up and wait, takeoff clearance, landing clearance, and go-around, and no other clearance kind. Each offer shall name the aircraft and the runway, and a sequenced aircraft shall also receive its position. Acceptance is one aircraft that can be assigned, queued, held short, lined up, cleared for takeoff or landing, and sent around, with any other kind refused.\n","RATIONALE":"Hold short, line up and wait, and go-around are required to keep the runway exclusive. The set is the tower subset of FAA JO 7110.65 used here.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SSS005"},"42":{"MID":"9a49cb1be7174ffa9d837d31d37a28fd","UID":"SSS006","TITLE":"Runways and their designations shall come from one TOML file per airport","STATEMENT":"Each airport shall be configured by one TOML file that names the airport, its position, communications distance, computer count, envelope bounds, and every runway. Each runway shall have an identifier, a designation of arrival, departure, both, or closed, and a flag stating whether it is independent of the other runways. The system shall not control traffic from a missing or invalid file. Acceptance is a file edit that closes a runway and a following assignment to that runway being refused.\n","RATIONALE":"The airport is meant to be retargeted by editing data, not by editing the clearance code.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SSS006"},"43":{"MID":"6b71b11b4828454cab78a9b7c49c2cb2","UID":"SSS007","TITLE":"Separation shall be demonstrated by a TLA+ model under stated assumptions and bounds","STATEMENT":"The separation invariant and the admissible clearance transitions shall be specified in TLA+ and checked with TLC on a finite model of at most 4 runways, 8 aircraft, and 2 neighbor airports. Every admissible transition in that model shall preserve exclusive protected volume, dependent-runway exclusion, and queue order, and shall refuse a neighbor-dependent clearance while the neighbor link is down. The software shall refuse to control a traffic picture outside that envelope. Acceptance is a TLC run that reports success on the checked model and a startup rejection above the envelope.\n","RATIONALE":"A finite model check is the formal evidence this increment can actually produce. Operation outside it is refused rather than implied to be proved.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Formal","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment. Aircraft performance is occupancy of one protected region at a time, with runway occupancy held until takeoff completes or the runway is vacated.","_LINK":"SSS007"},"44":{"MID":"1b6e1fcc7c7b41a1ae48c8811e74c525","UID":"SSS008","TITLE":"The Erlang service shall be tied to that model by a refinement argument","STATEMENT":"The Erlang clearance state shall be related to the TLA+ state by a written refinement mapping that names the corresponding variables and the assumptions it depends on, including the single ordered log. PropEr state-machine tests shall sample the Erlang transitions, including concurrent requests, process failure, recovery, and replica agreement, and those tests shall be recorded as conformance evidence rather than as a proof. Any obligation the mapping does not discharge shall stay labeled open. Acceptance is a mapping that a reader can check against the module and the spec, plus a test run that fails the build when a sampled transition breaks the invariant.\n","RATIONALE":"Testing does not establish implementation correctness. The mapping is the separate argument that connects the two descriptions.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Refinement","ASSUMPTIONS":"Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.","_LINK":"SSS008"},"45":{"MID":"ecb63b645b774e5683f7662663865576","UID":"SSS009","TITLE":"When n is greater than 1, one local computer failure shall leave a single clearance authority","STATEMENT":"When more than one computer is configured, clearances shall be appended to one ordered log and only a majority member that is the elected authority may append. After one computer fails, a surviving majority shall keep exactly one authority and the failed computer shall not issue clearances. For two computers the majority is both, so one failure stops clearances instead of leaving two authorities. Acceptance is a group of three where killing one leaves one authority, and a partition into one and two where only the side of two issues a clearance.\n","RATIONALE":"The safety claim is a single authority. Two computers cannot survive a failure without risking a split brain, so they stop.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.","_LINK":"SSS009"},"46":{"MID":"1f8e6d55c4594b14afe21541210d4d8a","UID":"SSS010","TITLE":"A clearance the separation guard rejects shall not be issued","STATEMENT":"The system shall apply the separation guard before it commits any clearance that changes runway occupancy, and it shall not put a rejected clearance on the ordered log as an issued clearance. The pilot-facing answer to a rejected request shall be a refusal that names the aircraft and the reason class. Acceptance is a request that would double-occupy a runway, with the log unchanged and the caller receiving a refusal.\n","RATIONALE":"The guard is useful only if a rejected transition never becomes the issued history.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"SSS010"},"47":{"MID":"4aa1c4d31be04e92a90a807a10e58ae7","UID":"STD001","TITLE":"TOML accept and reject cases","STATEMENT":"The test shall load the example airport TOML and expect a parsed airport with its runways, then load an empty file and a runway without a designation and expect both to be rejected before any clearance is issued. Acceptance is those three results, with the valid file producing a runway list and the two invalid files producing an error and no authority.\n","RATIONALE":"This is the example test for the configuration requirement.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The example file is config/example-airport.toml.","_LINK":"STD001"},"48":{"MID":"3b55a9a9ad194e349e5ac5f27863d3b7","UID":"STD002","TITLE":"Runway designation selection cases","STATEMENT":"The test shall attempt a landing on a departure-only runway, a takeoff on an arrival-only runway, an assignment to a closed runway, and a dual occupancy of two non-independent runways. Each attempt shall be refused. A landing on an empty both-use runway shall be accepted. Acceptance is those five outcomes.\n","RATIONALE":"Designation and independence are data, so the test supplies the data and checks the decision.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"STD002"},"49":{"MID":"af6dea0cd1d44f58a31c24ee4087f8d7","UID":"STD003","TITLE":"Group membership for one computer and for three","STATEMENT":"The test shall start a group with n equal to 1 and expect that member to be the authority, then start a group with n equal to 3 and expect a member that has not joined to refuse a clearance. Acceptance is authority on the single member and refusal from the unjoined member.\n","RATIONALE":"The rural case and the redundant case are both part of the same requirement.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.","_LINK":"STD003"},"50":{"MID":"7ca597fd12714de7936bd41bd9759d67","UID":"STD004","TITLE":"One clearance authority under a crash","STATEMENT":"The test shall start three log members, commit one clearance, stop one member, and expect the surviving majority to accept one further clearance while the stopped member accepts none. It shall also partition the three into a side of one and a side of two and expect only the side of two to accept a clearance. Acceptance is one committed clearance after the crash and a refusal from the minority side.\n","RATIONALE":"This is the example of a single authority after a local failure.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.","_LINK":"STD004"},"51":{"MID":"46db94e895844124ac78e5361166a6c7","UID":"STD005","TITLE":"Neighbor distance selection","STATEMENT":"The test shall place one candidate inside the communications distance and one outside it and expect only the inside candidate to be selected as a neighbor. Acceptance is a neighbor set of size one containing the inside airport.\n","RATIONALE":"The boundary is the configured distance, so the test uses positions on either side of it.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"Distance is computed in nautical miles.","_LINK":"STD005"},"52":{"MID":"4238ecfe32944b5f89597d2670589c6d","UID":"STD006","TITLE":"Handoff while the neighbor link is up","STATEMENT":"The test shall send a handoff to a neighbor whose link is up, accept it, and expect the aircraft to leave local control. A second handoff that the neighbor rejects shall leave the aircraft in local control. Acceptance is those two outcomes.\n","RATIONALE":"Accept and reject are the two answers the interface allows.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"STD006"},"53":{"MID":"0b97c12d8319427981a2f6315655beff","UID":"STD007","TITLE":"Partition fail-smart case","STATEMENT":"The test shall bring a neighbor link down, mark the neighbor picture stale, grant a local landing that the local guard allows, and refuse a handoff. It shall also show that the stale picture is not used to permit a second aircraft into a locally occupied volume. Acceptance is the granted local landing, the refused handoff, and the refused double occupancy.\n","RATIONALE":"Fail smart is continued local service plus refusal of dependent clearances.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"STD007"},"54":{"MID":"8bc3aff734ea4a1dbb58d930049a3de5","UID":"STD008","TITLE":"Queue, landing, takeoff, and runway assignment path","STATEMENT":"The test shall assign a both-use runway, sequence two aircraft, hold the second short, line the first up, clear the first for takeoff, and then clear the second to land only after the first is airborne. A landing attempted while the first still occupies the runway shall be refused. Acceptance is that ordered path and the one refusal.\n","RATIONALE":"One path covers assignment, sequence, hold short, line up and wait, takeoff, and landing together.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"STD008"},"55":{"MID":"33c477860db44622b82e174e8c1597cd","UID":"STD009","TITLE":"The guard refuses an unsafe clearance","STATEMENT":"The test shall submit a line-up for a second aircraft while the first occupies the runway and expect a refusal with the state unchanged. It shall then go around or complete the takeoff and expect the second line-up to be accepted. Acceptance is the refusal with an unchanged log prefix and the later acceptance.\n","RATIONALE":"The guard requirement is checked here by example, and by TLC and PropEr under the other descriptions.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"STD009"},"56":{"MID":"28aeabfa79e343778bca006f3fe2f873","UID":"STD010","TITLE":"PropEr state machine for concurrency, crash, recovery, and agreement","STATEMENT":"The PropEr state machine shall generate sequences of clearance commands, concurrent submissions, a member crash, and a restart that replays the log. Every accepted sequence shall preserve the exclusive-volume invariant, and every crashed member that restarts shall match the surviving log prefix before it accepts a new command. A failing property shall fail the build. Acceptance is a PropEr run of this module that passes, and a deliberate invariant break that fails the property.\n","RATIONALE":"These samples are conformance evidence. They are not a proof that the Erlang code refines the TLA+ spec.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"PropEr","ASSUMPTIONS":"Raft is assumed to deliver one ordered log and is not re-proved.","_LINK":"STD010"},"57":{"MID":"59e618acf0cc427db1503907ce4c4ed2","UID":"STD011","TITLE":"Bounds refusal","STATEMENT":"The test shall reject a configuration with 5 runways, reject a configuration that allows more than 8 aircraft, and reject the ninth aircraft at an airport already holding 8. Acceptance is those three refusals and no issued clearance in the first two cases.\n","RATIONALE":"The envelope is an operational limit, so the test sits just outside it.\n","DAL":"A","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The checked envelope is 4 runways, 8 aircraft under control, and 2 neighbor airports. Visual separation, LAHSO, radar vectoring, TRACON, enroute control, and wake RECAT are outside this increment.","_LINK":"STD011"},"58":{"MID":"a9dda66938a5432bbd54b505b42a4b2f","UID":"STD012","TITLE":"Audit trace contains the requirement UID","STATEMENT":"The test shall issue a landing and refuse an unsafe line-up, then read the audit. The landing record shall contain SRS011 and the refusal shall contain SRS013, along with the aircraft identity and the decision. Acceptance is both records present and no issued record for the refused line-up.\n","RATIONALE":"The audit is the product-side link from a decision back to the requirement.\n","DAL":"C","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"Audit records are operational, not debug prints.","_LINK":"STD012"},"59":{"MID":"b8405d18cbce43489f855281e923542c","UID":"STP001","TITLE":"Which SRS items are discharged by TLC, by refinement review, by PropEr, and by example tests","STATEMENT":"The test plan shall discharge SRS013 and SSS007 by TLC on AtcTower, SRS013 and SSS008 by review of the refinement mapping, SRS004 and SRS015 by PropEr state-machine tests, and the remaining software requirements by Common Test examples named in the software test description. A PropEr failure shall fail the build and shall not be rewritten as formal proof. Acceptance is a trace from each SRS item to one of those four methods, and a test run whose failing property stops the suite.\n","RATIONALE":"DO-178C wants the verification method named before the tests are treated as evidence.\n","DAL":"C","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Plan","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"TLC covers the finite model only. PropEr samples the implementation and does not prove it.","_LINK":"STP001"},"60":{"MID":"c1094b0cf1e049cd91caf67c90df996a","UID":"STR001","TITLE":"Record of the TLC run and the Common Test run","STATEMENT":"The test report shall record the commands that were actually run and the results they printed. On 2026-11-20, from the repository root, rebar3 as test ct reported All 15 tests passed, covering atc_config_SUITE, atc_clearance_SUITE, and atc_cluster_SUITE, and the last of those calls prop_clearance:quickcheck/0 with 40 cases. make tla-check reported no error on AtcTower, with 414 distinct states and depth 8. make run printed airport KEXAMPLE ready on 1 computers. The PropEr result is conformance evidence and is not a proof. Acceptance is this record matching those commands and results.\n","RATIONALE":"The report is written after the run, so the numbers are observations rather than a plan.\n","DAL":"C","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Plan","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"TLC covers the finite instance only. PropEr samples the Erlang state machine and does not prove refinement. No certification authority approval is claimed.","_LINK":"STR001"},"61":{"MID":"b00c154a77e34f22aae42c9bd10e6a9f","UID":"STrP001","TITLE":"Hand the release, the TOML, the model, and the open proof obligations to a support engineer","STATEMENT":"Transition to support shall hand over the release, the airport TOML file, the TLA+ model and its TLC result, the refinement mapping, and the list of open proof obligations. Support shall not be told that PropEr or TLC discharged an obligation the mapping still marks open. Acceptance is a handover list that contains those items and that repeats each open obligation in the same words as the mapping.\n","RATIONALE":"The support engineer needs the limit of the evidence, not only the binaries.\n","DAL":"D","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Plan","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"STrP is the MIL-STD-498 software transition plan. It is not the software test report.","_LINK":"STrP001"},"62":{"MID":"47642bd70481459b98d84ae6ec1a3042","UID":"SUM001","TITLE":"Start, stop, and edit runway designations for one airport","STATEMENT":"The operator manual shall tell an operator how to edit runway designations in the airport TOML file, start the n local computers, and stop them. It shall state that a closed runway will not be assigned and that a file outside the checked envelope will not start. Acceptance is a manual section that names the TOML keys for designation and the start and stop commands, and an operator who can close a runway by editing the file and restarting.\n","RATIONALE":"The user of this CSCI is the airport operator who maintains the TOML file, not a pilot.\n","DAL":"C","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Plan","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The manual does not restate FAA JO 7110.65.","_LINK":"SUM001"},"63":{"MID":"300a3f1e57ef43af9bfb9a2d7131245b","UID":"SVD001","TITLE":"Version 0.1.0 of the tower CSCI","STATEMENT":"The version description shall identify atc_tower 0.1.0, dated 2026-11-20, as the rebar3 release of the Tower CSCI together with AtcTower.tla, the refinement mapping, the StrictDoc sources, and the HTML generated under reqs/html. It shall record the TLC result of 414 distinct states with no invariant error and the Common Test result of 15 passing tests. Acceptance is a version record that names those artifacts and results and does not claim certification authority approval.\n","RATIONALE":"The version description freezes the evidence that belongs to release 0.1.0.\n","DAL":"C","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Plan","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"reqs/html is produced by make strictdoc-generate from the StrictDoc sources. PropEr remains conformance evidence.","_LINK":"SVD001"},"64":{"MID":"4a4a64d2ca55459e9aa7d9c4717deb6d","UID":"AC-IDD001","TITLE":"In-memory transmission and link events, with encoding deferred","STATEMENT":"The concrete port shall be an in-memory object. send shall return sent, blocked, or down. A sent transmission shall appear on the outbound list. A blocked transmission shall not. The aircraft shall pass Transmission values and LinkEvent values for delivered, blocked, garbled, down, and up. No byte encoding shall be implemented. Acceptance is one blocked ATIS request that still results in a single outbound copy, and a second block pair that leaves the outbound list unchanged.\n","RATIONALE":"The in-memory port is the stand-in until a later plan selects a method.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-IDD001"},"65":{"MID":"def95c903a634800892bc6dd4f7cc364","UID":"AC-IRS001","TITLE":"Transmission content for a pattern exchange","STATEMENT":"A transmission shall be able to carry the facility, the full call sign, the registration, an optional position, the phrase kind, the runway identifier, a sequence number, an ATIS letter, a frequency in megahertz, the next facility, the emergency nature, the intention, and whether a taxi clearance includes hold short. Wind and altimeter may arrive on an inbound clearance and shall not be copied into the readback. Acceptance is a landing clearance whose runway and kind survive parsing and whose readback contains neither wind nor altimeter.\n","RATIONALE":"The fields are the information content. The phrase is their spoken form.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Interface","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-IRS001"},"66":{"MID":"2fed0c153cc34e7d924a9427c956561a","UID":"AC-IRS002","TITLE":"Link events for delivery and faults","STATEMENT":"The link shall report delivered when a transmission reaches the peer, blocked when an outbound transmission does not, garbled when an inbound transmission cannot be used, and down and up when the link changes state. A garble shall say whether it was addressed to this aircraft. Acceptance is a blocked send that is absent from the peer queue and an addressed garble that produces Say again.\n","RATIONALE":"The events are how the aircraft learns the port state without a radio model.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Interface","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-IRS002"},"67":{"MID":"382559abd9e5499c82c164d78540cfac","UID":"AC-IRS003","TITLE":"Aircraft and airport TOML schema","STATEMENT":"The configuration file shall contain exactly the tables aircraft, performance, airport, runway, ramp, and option. aircraft shall carry n_number, facility, next_facility, and next_frequency_mhz in the range 118.000 to 136.975. performance shall carry taxi, rotation, and pattern speeds in increasing order, pattern altitude, takeoff and landing distances, turn rate, acceleration, vertical speed, and a low-approach height below pattern altitude. runway shall carry an identifier from 01 through 36 with optional L, C, or R, a heading from 0 through 359, length, left or right pattern, hold-short distance, pattern offset, and an upwind distance beyond the departure end. option.choice shall be full_stop, touch_and_go, stop_and_go, or low_approach. Extra keys and missing keys shall be errors. Acceptance is config/n123ab.toml loading and an empty file, a bad pattern, and a frequency of 100.0 being rejected.\n","RATIONALE":"One closed schema keeps a misspelled key from looking like a valid aircraft.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Interface","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-IRS003"},"68":{"MID":"484df31fb01446cda09f919074030005","UID":"AC-IRS004","TITLE":"Phrase text is the notation and byte encoding is not selected","STATEMENT":"The normative external notation of a transmission shall be the rendered phrase string. The in-memory port shall pass the transmission object and that phrase. No radio modulation, socket framing, or line encoding shall be selected in this increment. Acceptance is a round trip of a rendered request back to the same kind, runway, and registration, with the phrase unchanged.\n","RATIONALE":"A later plan can choose a carriage without rewriting the phrase set.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Interface","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-IRS004"},"69":{"MID":"c25d217396314f8c9f538d50eaeae634","UID":"AC-OCD001","TITLE":"One configured civil aircraft flies a local pattern at one configured airport","STATEMENT":"The operational concept shall be one fictional civil aircraft, identified by one configured N-number, operating at one airport that has one runway and one pattern direction. The aircraft shall be able to move from the ramp through taxi, hold short, line up and wait, takeoff, a closed pattern, and a landing, option, touch-and-go, stop-and-go, or low approach chosen by configuration. Acceptance is a concept in which that single aircraft completes the pattern without a second aircraft, a second runway, LAHSO, or an intersection departure.\n","RATIONALE":"The mock exists to practice one pattern, not to simulate a fleet or a metroplex.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Operational","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-OCD001"},"70":{"MID":"be2c04a7b7af49e4916ed79504763cb5","UID":"AC-OCD002","TITLE":"The pilot speaks FAA phraseology through a link whose method is not chosen","STATEMENT":"The pilot shall exchange the local-pattern requests, reports, and readbacks with the tower by FAA phraseology. The concept shall name the AIM and JO 7110.65 as the authority for the order of that speech and shall leave the radio, socket, or other carrying method unselected. Acceptance is a concept in which every operational exchange can be read as a phrase while no wire format is required to understand it.\n","RATIONALE":"The words are the operational interface. The carriage can be chosen later.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Operational","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-OCD002"},"71":{"MID":"8cf7e4d456384a8db8b2944785b9b8e3","UID":"AC-OCD003","TITLE":"The spoken position matches the point-mass state","STATEMENT":"When the pilot reports a position or includes a position in a call, the words shall describe the aircraft point-mass state at that moment, including the pattern leg when the aircraft is on one and the distance and direction when it is not. Acceptance is a concept in which a reader of the phrase log can tell the leg or the distance that the model occupied when the phrase was sent.\n","RATIONALE":"A phrase that names the wrong place is not a usable mock.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Operational","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-OCD003"},"72":{"MID":"de7b1e6ab3a54395b9ab84f8e0f8278b","UID":"AC-OCD004","TITLE":"A blocked, garbled, or lost link does not create a clearance","STATEMENT":"A lost link, a blocked transmission, or a garbled transmission shall not by itself give the aircraft a new clearance. The aircraft shall keep flying the last clearance it had already accepted, and it shall ask for a repeat or repeat its own call only when the link can still carry speech. Acceptance is a concept in which a fault leaves the last accepted maneuver in force and adds no new runway clearance.\n","RATIONALE":"The mock must not treat silence or noise as a clearance.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Operational","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-OCD004"},"73":{"MID":"77b83e32804e4a99b7e1b298485bbdd3","UID":"AC-OCD005","TITLE":"The pilot may declare Mayday or Pan-Pan without an answer","STATEMENT":"The pilot shall be able to declare Mayday or Pan-Pan in the standard repeated form, including the facility, the call sign, the nature, the current position, and the intention. The concept shall not require the tower to answer, and the declaration itself shall not change the maneuver. Acceptance is a declaration that can be read from the phrase log with no following tower transmission.\n","RATIONALE":"This increment declares the emergency and stops there.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Operational","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-OCD005"},"74":{"MID":"c377f5979d5446d0b1e17a6d03d9a00e","UID":"AC-SDD001","TITLE":"Objects and which one owns step, receive, and request","STATEMENT":"The Aircraft object shall own the call sign, the phase, the last clearance, the decision log, the phrase log, and the methods step, receive, and the request helpers. PointMass shall own the kinematic state and shall integrate only when Aircraft.step calls it. The phrase book shall render and parse. The link shall only store events and deliveries. A request or a receive shall not by itself change position. Acceptance is a taxi clearance that leaves position unchanged until step, and a later step that moves a taxiing aircraft.\n","RATIONALE":"The ownership split keeps motion out of the phrase methods.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SDD001"},"75":{"MID":"3137980717a24dcbaed11e7fc3c328cd","UID":"AC-SDD002","TITLE":"Phase machine and the clearance that enables each transition","STATEMENT":"The phases shall be ramp, taxi, hold short, line up, takeoff roll, climb, crosswind, downwind, base, final, rollout, stopped, and go-around. Taxi shall be accepted from ramp or taxi. Hold short shall be accepted from taxi, hold short, or line up. Line up and wait shall be accepted from hold short. Takeoff shall be accepted only from line up after alignment. Landing, the option, touch-and-go, stop-and-go, and go-around shall be accepted only while airborne. Sequence, runway assignment, and frequency change shall be accepted in any phase and shall not change the phase by themselves. Any other combination shall be Unable. Acceptance is a takeoff clearance refused on the ramp's legal successor hold-short until the aircraft has lined up, and accepted once it has.\n","RATIONALE":"The legal phase is what keeps a clearance from skipping the pattern.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SDD002"},"76":{"MID":"96b2e36ace7a490589288ad204cf8111","UID":"AC-SDD003","TITLE":"Point-mass integration and the rectangular pattern","STATEMENT":"The local frame shall put the runway threshold at the origin. Heading zero shall be north and shall increase clockwise. The hold-short point shall be the configured distance before the threshold. Line up shall be 100 feet past the threshold. The crosswind corner shall be the upwind distance ahead and the pattern offset to the pattern side. The downwind end and the final intercept shall be one pattern offset before the threshold. Capture inside a step shall place the aircraft on a reached waypoint. On final, target altitude shall follow a straight glide from pattern altitude to field elevation, except a low approach whose target is the configured height. Acceptance is a deterministic one-second step and a pattern mission that reaches the downwind and then the new facility.\n","RATIONALE":"The geometry is simple so the phrase and the position stay tied together.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SDD003"},"77":{"MID":"bc5f0daf6ef14a54bb12da5a7d220f2b","UID":"AC-SDD004","TITLE":"One renderer and one parser for the closed phrase set","STATEMENT":"Phrase rendering and parsing shall live in one module. The parser shall accept the renderer output and the tower clearances for taxi with hold short, hold short, line up and wait, takeoff, landing, go-around, sequence, runway assignment, frequency change, the option, touch-and-go, stop-and-go, and an information letter. It shall strip a wind clause and an altimeter clause before matching. Acceptance is a round trip of the ATIS request, the pattern-entry request, the landing request, and the takeoff readback, each returning the same kind and registration.\n","RATIONALE":"A second copy of the phrase set would drift.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SDD004"},"78":{"MID":"970cfafdbce744f6a9d7f242970eee7b","UID":"AC-SDP001","TITLE":"Lifecycle, DID set, DAL E, Python, deferred transport, and trace rules","STATEMENT":"The Aircraft CSCI software development plan shall record lifecycle data with the Software development plan (SDP), Software installation plan (SIP), Software transition plan (STrP), Operational concept description (OCD), System/subsystem specification (SSS), Software requirements specification (SRS), Interface requirements specification (IRS), System/subsystem design description (SSDD), Software design description (SDD), Database design description (DBDD), Interface design description (IDD), Software test plan (STP), Software test description (STD), Software test report (STR), Software user manual (SUM), Software product specification (SPS), and Software version description (SVD). Every aircraft requirement shall be DAL E. The implementation language shall be Python. The method that carries phraseology to the tower shall remain unselected. Each fragment shall name its parents, and each implementing source file shall name the requirement UID in a comment and in the commit that adds it. Acceptance is this record, with no claim of certification authority approval.\n","RATIONALE":"The plan is the contract for which descriptions exist and how a change points back at a requirement.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Plan","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"Phraseology names the AIM and JO 7110.65 and does not copy their tables. The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SDP001"},"79":{"MID":"c4086a1bd6ce4f79832b6bdca26fd87b","UID":"AC-SDP002","TITLE":"SIOM, SCOM, COM, CPM, and FSM tailored out, with reasons","STATEMENT":"The aircraft plan shall tailor out the Software input/output manual (SIOM), the Software center operator manual (SCOM), the Computer operation manual (COM), the Computer programming manual (CPM), and the Firmware support manual (FSM). SIOM is absent because the only persistent input is the aircraft TOML file and the phrase log stays in memory. SCOM and COM are absent because there is no computer-center operator and no separate computer operations procedure. CPM is absent because the design description and the Python sources are the programming record. FSM is absent because the aircraft has no firmware. Acceptance is this record of those five exclusions and no other DID removed from the set.\n","RATIONALE":"MIL-STD-498 expects the contract to say which descriptions were not ordered.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Plan","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SDP002"},"80":{"MID":"78976ef79d5442589de8e2fd691c75c1","UID":"AC-SRS001","TITLE":"Reject invalid TOML and do not fly","STATEMENT":"Before an aircraft flies, the CSCI shall read its TOML file and shall refuse to construct the aircraft when the file is missing, unreadable, or fails the AC-IRS003 schema. Acceptance is the example file producing an aircraft for N123AB, and an empty file, a missing registration, a pattern value outside left or right, and a frequency of 100.0 each raising a configuration error with no aircraft object.\n","RATIONALE":"A bad file is not a flyable aircraft.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS001"},"81":{"MID":"f94610c4135942a4bb26e9c9ee72704f","UID":"AC-SRS002","TITLE":"Speak the full N-number on every transmission","STATEMENT":"The CSCI shall speak the configured registration on every transmission it sends. N123AB shall be November one two three alpha bravo. Digit 9 shall be niner and digit 0 shall be zero. A registration with a leading zero, the letters I or O, or lowercase letters shall be rejected. Acceptance is that spoken form and the rejection of N0123, N123I, and n123ab.\n","RATIONALE":"The full form is the only call sign this increment sends.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS002"},"82":{"MID":"6957b42ea29f43fe90f8310fb7449f77","UID":"AC-SRS003","TITLE":"Render requests as facility, call sign, position, request","STATEMENT":"A request shall be rendered as the facility, the full call sign, the position when the call is an initial contact or a position report, and then the request, separated by commas and ended with a period. An ATIS request shall omit the position. A pattern-entry request that already has the information letter shall include with information and the phonetic letter. Acceptance is the ATIS request for Example Tower and N123AB, and the pattern-entry request from the ramp with information alpha, both parsing back to the same kind and registration.\n","RATIONALE":"One renderer is the source of the request order.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS003"},"83":{"MID":"10b3fd2d01d444e99b9dddc73183a010","UID":"AC-SRS004","TITLE":"Render readbacks as the operative clearance, then the call sign","STATEMENT":"A readback shall be rendered as the operative clearance and then the full call sign. Wind and altimeter present on the inbound clearance shall be omitted. The pilot wording for a go-around instruction shall be Going around. Acceptance is a takeoff clearance that includes wind and altimeter and reads back as Cleared for takeoff runway two seven followed by the call sign, with neither wind nor altimeter in the readback.\n","RATIONALE":"The readback repeats the clearance elements the AIM treats as the check.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS004"},"84":{"MID":"8b0c82a24ecc4b248a6d0f4a7d553b71","UID":"AC-SRS005","TITLE":"Request ATIS or include the information letter","STATEMENT":"The aircraft shall be able to request ATIS. When a peer answers with an information letter, the aircraft shall store that letter and a following pattern-entry call shall include it in phonetic form. The information transmission itself shall not be read back and shall not move the aircraft. Acceptance is an ATIS request, storage of letter A from Information alpha, and a pattern-entry phrase that says with information alpha.\n","RATIONALE":"The initial call carries the letter the pilot has already received.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS005"},"85":{"MID":"e2c68725e752456e96a7764c7e17d9d5","UID":"AC-SRS006","TITLE":"Request taxi and read back the taxi clearance","STATEMENT":"From the ramp the aircraft shall request taxi to its configured runway. A taxi clearance that includes hold short shall be read back with both the taxi instruction and the hold-short runway, and the aircraft shall then taxi toward the hold-short point. The position shall not change until step is called. Acceptance is the readback Taxi to runway two seven, hold short runway two seven, followed by the call sign, and a later stop at the hold-short point.\n","RATIONALE":"Taxi is the first ground maneuver and the readback has to include the hold.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS006"},"86":{"MID":"177b7b6463644131909096387911ff31","UID":"AC-SRS007","TITLE":"Report holding short and read back a hold-short instruction","STATEMENT":"When the aircraft is holding short it shall be able to report that fact with the runway. A hold-short instruction addressed to this runway shall be read back as Hold short runway and the spoken runway, then the call sign. If the aircraft is lined up and is then told to hold short, it shall return to the hold-short point and stop. Acceptance is the report Example Tower, the call sign, holding short runway two seven.\n","RATIONALE":"Hold short is both a report and a readback, and the runway is part of both.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS007"},"87":{"MID":"e61b4c1c9c4d4f35af575659761f32d3","UID":"AC-SRS008","TITLE":"Read back line up and wait, align, and wait","STATEMENT":"From hold short, a line-up-and-wait clearance shall be read back as Line up and wait runway and the spoken runway, then the call sign. The aircraft shall taxi onto the runway to 100 feet past the threshold, align with the runway heading, and stop. It shall not begin the takeoff roll until a takeoff clearance. Acceptance is that readback and a stopped, aligned aircraft still in the line-up phase.\n","RATIONALE":"Line up and wait is not a takeoff clearance.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS008"},"88":{"MID":"6e096fe983f34f138d29524d8811afae","UID":"AC-SRS009","TITLE":"Report ready, read back takeoff, and fly the roll and climb","STATEMENT":"The aircraft shall be able to report holding short and ready for takeoff. After it is lined up and stopped, a takeoff clearance shall be read back as Cleared for takeoff runway and the spoken runway, then the call sign. The aircraft shall accelerate, rotate at the configured rotation speed, and climb on runway heading toward pattern altitude. Acceptance is that readback, a climb phase, and a takeoff roll that stays on the runway centerline.\n","RATIONALE":"Takeoff is accepted only after the aircraft is lined up and waiting.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS009"},"89":{"MID":"70e773e432c0430fb5dce2127dd392c7","UID":"AC-SRS010","TITLE":"Request pattern entry and landing, and read back runway and landing","STATEMENT":"The aircraft shall request pattern entry for the configured pattern side and runway, and shall request landing with its current position. A runway assignment and a cleared-to-land clearance for this runway shall be read back with the runway and the call sign last. The aircraft shall not descend to the surface on final until a landing clearance or another landing-type clearance is accepted. Acceptance is the pattern-entry phrase from the ramp and the readback Cleared to land runway two seven followed by the call sign.\n","RATIONALE":"Landing is a separate acceptance from merely flying the pattern.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS010"},"90":{"MID":"3ae7bea0468644ef98bf49075061d37a","UID":"AC-SRS011","TITLE":"Fly and say going around for a pilot or controller go-around","STATEMENT":"A pilot-initiated go-around while airborne shall be spoken as the facility, the call sign, and going around, and shall start the climb. A controller instruction Go around shall be read back as Going around and then the call sign, and shall start the same climb on runway heading toward pattern altitude and then the crosswind. The go-around shall cancel a landing clearance. Acceptance is both phrases and a go-around phase whose altitude does not decrease.\n","RATIONALE":"The pilot word is going around. The controller word is go around.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS011"},"91":{"MID":"8b5d5d72a4744bdd87050687c7ff8568","UID":"AC-SRS012","TITLE":"Read back the sequence number","STATEMENT":"A sequence instruction shall be read back as Number and the spoken digits, including the runway when the instruction names one, and then the call sign. The sequence shall be stored and shall not change phase, position, or speed. Acceptance is Number two, runway two seven, followed by the call sign, with the maneuver unchanged.\n","RATIONALE":"Sequence is information. It is not a clearance to move.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS012"},"92":{"MID":"ad7807c4975d440ebabbd9bd522f7fdc","UID":"AC-SRS013","TITLE":"Read back a frequency change and address the new facility","STATEMENT":"The aircraft shall be able to request a frequency change. A contact instruction shall be read back as the spoken frequency and then the call sign, without the wind or the facility name in the readback. Subsequent transmissions shall address the new facility. The maneuver shall not change. Acceptance is the readback one two four point five followed by the call sign, and a later request that begins with Departure.\n","RATIONALE":"The frequency is the readback. The new facility is the next call.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS013"},"93":{"MID":"adea71ee368043799a35af1c7ccea8b5","UID":"AC-SRS014","TITLE":"Build position reports from the dynamics state","STATEMENT":"A position clause shall come from the current phase and point-mass state. On the ramp it shall say at the ramp. While taxiing, holding short, lined up, on the runway, or stopped, it shall name that condition and the runway. In climb or go-around it shall say upwind. Crosswind, downwind, and base shall include the pattern side. Final shall say final. Altitude shall be rounded to the nearest 100 feet and spoken as thousands and hundreds, with 9 as niner. A distance under 100 feet from the threshold shall be at the field. A distance that rounds to zero nautical miles shall be less than one mile. Other distances shall be individual digits and miles or mile, plus the eight-point compass. Pattern altitude shall be joined with at. Acceptance is upwind runway two seven at one thousand, left downwind at one thousand five hundred, and one zero miles east at one thousand.\n","RATIONALE":"The rounding rules make the phrase testable.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS014"},"94":{"MID":"94a2e164917a4468842ab601444699ff","UID":"AC-SRS015","TITLE":"Request and fly the option, touch-and-go, and stop-and-go","STATEMENT":"The aircraft shall request the option, touch-and-go, or stop-and-go and shall read back the matching clearance with the runway and the call sign last. Touch-and-go shall touch and become airborne again. Stop-and-go shall land, slow, and then roll for takeoff. A cleared-for-the-option clearance shall fly the configured choice, and low approach shall descend only to the configured height above the field and then climb without landing. A landing clearance shall full-stop. Acceptance is a touch-and-go that reaches the surface and rolls again, a stop-and-go that slows below 5 knots and then accelerates, and a low approach that stays at or above 150 feet.\n","RATIONALE":"The option outcome is configured so the flight is repeatable.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS015"},"95":{"MID":"170b205354be4f77b4eb6e024efe9813","UID":"AC-SRS016","TITLE":"Say Unable and keep the previous maneuver","STATEMENT":"The aircraft shall say Unable, the refused clearance in lowercase operative words, and the full call sign, when a takeoff runway is shorter than takeoff_distance_ft, a landing-type runway is shorter than landing_distance_ft, or the phase does not allow the clearance. It shall not change phase or speed because of that refusal. Another call sign or another runway shall produce no phrase and no Unable decision. Acceptance is Unable cleared for takeoff runway two seven on an 800 foot runway while the aircraft stays lined up and stopped, and silence for N999ZZ and for runway 28.\n","RATIONALE":"Unable is the speech. The previous maneuver is what continues.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS016"},"96":{"MID":"4275b727e03c42e9948fdad2c38a3ca4","UID":"AC-SRS017","TITLE":"On link down, send nothing and continue the last maneuver","STATEMENT":"When the link reports down, further requests, readbacks, repeats, and emergency declarations shall not be sent. A taxi already accepted shall continue on later time steps. A clearance delivered while the link is down shall not be accepted. Acceptance is a down event during taxi after which the phrase log does not grow, an emergency call adds no phrase, and the aircraft is still taxiing farther along the path.\n","RATIONALE":"The last accepted clearance remains the only maneuver.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS017"},"97":{"MID":"a34b21c07c094edaaf10756850889bf3","UID":"AC-SRS018","TITLE":"On an addressed garble, say again and do not accept it","STATEMENT":"An addressed garbled event shall cause the phrase Say again followed by the full call sign and shall not change the phase. A garble that is not addressed to this aircraft shall produce no phrase. Acceptance is exactly one Say again phrase and a ramp phase that is unchanged.\n","RATIONALE":"An unreadable clearance is not a clearance.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS018"},"98":{"MID":"953f473607544b39bfa0764a0c722fa8","UID":"AC-SRS019","TITLE":"On a blocked transmission, repeat it once","STATEMENT":"When the port reports that a send was blocked, the aircraft shall send the same transmission one more time. If that repeat is also blocked, the aircraft shall stop. The peer shall receive only the copy that was not blocked. Acceptance is one delivered ATIS request after a single block, and a taxi request that is absent from the peer queue when two consecutive sends are blocked.\n","RATIONALE":"One repeat is the bound. A second block ends the attempt.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS019"},"99":{"MID":"1f4e6016fbf4459c9544560c14f3de05","UID":"AC-SRS020","TITLE":"Declare Mayday or Pan-Pan with nature, position, and intention","STATEMENT":"declare_emergency shall send Mayday three times or Pan-Pan three times, then the facility, the full call sign, the nature, the current position, and the intention. The phase and speed shall stay as they were. Acceptance is the ramp Mayday for engine failure and landing runway two seven, a Pan-Pan that starts with the word three times, and a ramp phase that is still stopped.\n","RATIONALE":"The declaration is a phrase. It is not a new maneuver.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS020"},"100":{"MID":"17ec793f89774c299ed4dbd07bcc6b13","UID":"AC-SRS021","TITLE":"Advance motion only through a deterministic step","STATEMENT":"Aircraft.step shall be the only aircraft operation that moves the point mass. Inside a step the model shall turn toward the target heading or the waypoint, change speed toward the target speed, set vertical speed toward the target altitude within the configured limit, and then integrate position. A non-positive time step shall be rejected and shall not change state. The same inputs shall produce the same next state. Automatic captures, including arrival at hold short, rotation, and pattern-leg changes, shall occur inside step. Acceptance is an unchanged state after a zero time step and matching states after one one-second step on two copies of the model.\n","RATIONALE":"Deterministic time is what makes the flight repeatable.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS021"},"101":{"MID":"24871df1486f437db6b7fce6a5cdd82f","UID":"AC-SRS022","TITLE":"Record the UID that authorized a decision","STATEMENT":"The aircraft shall append an in-memory decision record for each accepted clearance, refusal, link-down transition, garble response, blocked repeat, emergency declaration, and automatic phase change. The record shall name the requirement UID and a one-line summary. A step that does not change phase shall not add a record. The log shall not be written to disk. Acceptance is a takeoff sequence whose log contains AC-SRS021 after a phase change, and an Unable decision whose log contains AC-SRS016.\n","RATIONALE":"The log is the in-memory trace from a decision back to a requirement.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"High-Level","VERIFICATION":"Test","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SRS022"},"102":{"MID":"bd38f706d5b747279ca448ecebd5aa25","UID":"AC-SSDD001","TITLE":"The aircraft, one runway, and the tower as an external system","STATEMENT":"The system design shall contain one aircraft, one runway, the ramp, and the pattern geometry, and shall treat the tower as an external peer. The only failure domain inside this CSCI shall be the phraseology link. A down, blocked, or garbled link shall not be described as a failure of the tower computers. Acceptance is a design trace that names the link events and does not assign tower failover behavior to this CSCI.\n","RATIONALE":"This CSCI does not operate the tower and does not share its computers.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"Low-Level","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SSDD001"},"103":{"MID":"0c7238480bf143849e477615263d99fe","UID":"AC-SSS001","TITLE":"Accepted clearances shall drive the point-mass maneuver","STATEMENT":"When the aircraft accepts a clearance that authorizes taxi, hold short, line up and wait, takeoff, landing, go-around, the option, touch-and-go, or stop-and-go, the point-mass model shall fly that maneuver and shall not begin it before acceptance. A request alone shall not move the aircraft. Acceptance is a taxi clearance whose position is unchanged until the next time step and whose later steps follow the taxi path to the hold-short point.\n","RATIONALE":"The maneuver and the clearance have to be the same story.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SSS001"},"104":{"MID":"4e13f98f3a914c21b3032c5453aee2dd","UID":"AC-SSS002","TITLE":"Requests and readbacks shall cover the pattern set in AIM order","STATEMENT":"The system shall be able to request or report ATIS, pattern entry, taxi, hold short, ready for takeoff, landing, go-around, frequency change, position, the option, touch-and-go, and stop-and-go, and shall read back runway assignment, sequence, hold short, line up and wait, takeoff, landing, go-around, frequency, the option, touch-and-go, and stop-and-go. A request shall be spoken as facility, full call sign, position when the call is initial or is a position report, then the request. A readback shall be spoken as the operative clearance and then the full call sign. Acceptance is one rendered request and one rendered readback in that order for runway 27 and N123AB.\n","RATIONALE":"The order is the FAA convention this mock is required to follow.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SSS002"},"105":{"MID":"a4c34e9d9b764ea2aa6a523d225a0b80","UID":"AC-SSS003","TITLE":"Every transmission shall use the one full spoken N-number","STATEMENT":"Every transmission the aircraft sends shall contain the full spoken form of its one configured civil N-number. Digits shall be spoken individually, with 9 spoken as niner and 0 spoken as zero, and letters shall use the ICAO radiotelephony alphabet. The aircraft shall not shorten the call sign. Acceptance is N123AB spoken as November one two three alpha bravo on a request and on a readback.\n","RATIONALE":"Abbreviation waits until a later increment that has a tower using the short form.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SSS003"},"106":{"MID":"7611b9c3db4e4be99f61a281d503f1c7","UID":"AC-SSS004","TITLE":"A clearance outside performance or legal phase shall be refused","STATEMENT":"When a clearance is addressed to this aircraft and this runway but the runway is shorter than the configured takeoff or landing distance, or the current phase cannot legally accept that clearance, the aircraft shall say Unable and shall keep the previous maneuver. A transmission for another call sign or another runway shall be ignored and shall not produce Unable. Acceptance is a takeoff clearance on an 800 foot runway, after line up and wait, that is refused while the aircraft remains lined up and stopped.\n","RATIONALE":"The mock must refuse what its performance and phase cannot fly.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SSS004"},"107":{"MID":"61495aa6aec74e5c89d01226779527d3","UID":"AC-SSS005","TITLE":"A lost link shall preserve the last accepted clearance","STATEMENT":"When the link is down, the aircraft shall not originate a request, a readback, a repeat, or an emergency call. It shall keep the last clearance it had already accepted and shall continue that maneuver. A clearance offered while the link is down shall not become accepted. With no accepted taxi or takeoff clearance, the aircraft shall remain stopped on the ground. Acceptance is a taxi already in progress that continues after the link goes down, and a new request that adds no phrase.\n","RATIONALE":"Silence is not a new instruction.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SSS005"},"108":{"MID":"c70645ef720e42f58be0851c470dbd68","UID":"AC-SSS006","TITLE":"A garbled transmission is queried and a blocked one is repeated once","STATEMENT":"An addressed garbled transmission shall not be accepted. The aircraft shall say Say again followed by the full call sign. A garbled transmission that is not addressed to this aircraft shall be ignored. When the port reports that an outbound transmission was blocked, the aircraft shall send that same transmission once more and shall not continue repeating if the repeat is also blocked. Acceptance is one Say again phrase and one delivered copy of a transmission whose first send was blocked.\n","RATIONALE":"The fault behavior is bounded so a blocked port cannot loop.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SSS006"},"109":{"MID":"eb3b56f7c39e47d9bee2fa8e93f3a81d","UID":"AC-SSS007","TITLE":"Mayday and Pan-Pan shall be declared in standard form","STATEMENT":"On request, the aircraft shall declare Mayday or Pan-Pan by repeating the word three times and then speaking the facility, the full call sign, the nature, the current position, and the intention. The declaration shall not change phase, speed, or the accepted maneuver. No tower reply shall be required. Acceptance is a Mayday from the ramp whose phrase carries the nature and intention and whose phase remains ramp.\n","RATIONALE":"The declaration is speech only in this increment.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SSS007"},"110":{"MID":"1989992c0ac84afea378e5556fcf23b5","UID":"AC-SSS008","TITLE":"The port shall carry content and phrase text and shall not select an encoding","STATEMENT":"The port between the aircraft and a peer shall carry the transmission fields and the rendered phrase. It shall also carry the events delivered, blocked, garbled, down, and up. It shall not select a radio, socket, line format, or other byte encoding. Acceptance is an in-memory delivery of one phrase that a peer can read, with no encoded frame around it.\n","RATIONALE":"The encoding is an open decision recorded here so a later plan can choose it.\n","DAL":"E","REQUIREMENT_LEVEL":"System","VERIFICATION":"Review","ASSUMPTIONS":"The Aircraft CSCI is a simulation. It is not connected to a real aircraft or a live facility, and this record does not claim certification authority approval.","_LINK":"AC-SSS008"}};
